## SCSS Structure

```
lms/static/sass/
├── lms-main-v1.scss            ← main LMS stylesheet entry point
├── base/
│   ├── _base.scss              ← .content-wrapper base rule (centering, max-width)
│   └── _layouts.scss           ← page-specific overrides (e.g. body.view-index)
├── bootstrap/
│   └── _layouts.scss           ← Bootstrap variant of .content-wrapper
├── shared/
│   └── _footer.scss            ← footer styles (.wrapper-logo, .innovation-fond-logo)
└── _variables.scss             ← SCSS variables ($baseline, $container-max-widths, etc.)
```

After any SCSS change, recompile on the remote server:
```bash
tutor local run lms python manage.py lms compile_sass
```

---

## Comprehensive Theming

Implemented in `openedx/core/djangoapps/theming/`.

- Theme directory mirrors the repo tree: `themes/<name>/lms/templates/` and `themes/<name>/lms/static/`
- `SiteTheme` model maps a Django `Site` to a theme directory name
- `CurrentSiteThemeMiddleware` attaches the active theme to each request
- `ThemeTemplateLoader` prepends the theme's template dir to the search path
- `compile_sass` management command compiles per-theme SCSS

